## Chain audit

[JUDGEMENT] The 5-step chain is INCOMPLETE as stated, not sound: step 3 ("mixing ⇒ nowhere to hide") has no transfer lemma. Mixing here is a typical-start statement; a single exceptional orbit is compatible with perfect typical mixing. B1 is exactly this gap, and B2 bites at step 4→3 even if the target inequality is proved (a family of finite statements still needs a uniform limit argument that is unwritten).

## B1: formalisation and verdict — PARTIAL

- B1-weak [PROOF]: density-1 ⇏ all. Trivial logic.
- B1-medium [PROOF]: Lᵖ-averaged bounds (Ecal, discrepancy, averaged Fourier) are stable under density-0 changes, so no such bound BY ITSELF excludes one orbit/cycle. Airtight — the true core.
- B1-strong [JUDGEMENT/CONJECTURE]: "no mixing-based programme can ever reach every-case." Not a theorem; false as a universal.
- [JUDGEMENT] Counter-patterns exist where mixing + rigidity gives every-case: (a) uniform-hitting + descent ⇒ infinite descent; (b) analytic bound + finite check; (c) cycle equation + transcendence (Steiner 1-cycles; Simons–de Weger-type lower bounds — qualitative pattern high-confidence, constants deliberately not quoted); (d) expansion ⇒ deterministic hitting (with the programme's own Fourier ≥1/2 obstruction constraining which gap to ask for). What "something else" must be here: a uniform hitting/covering lemma + descent lemma, or an explicit bridge bound — none owned today.
- Verdict: PARTIAL (FATAL to averaging-alone, OVERSTATED as universal). Confidence HIGH on logic, MEDIUM on whether the rigid ingredient exists for divergence.

## B2: formalisation and verdict — PARTIAL (FATAL in-scope, OVERSTATED out-of-scope)

- B2-weak [PROOF]: ∀m∃n ⇏ ∃n∀m. Finite realisability ≠ global realiser.
- B2-medium [PROOF, standard]: compactness gives a 2-adic realiser (Z₂), not an N-realiser. The honest wall is Z₂⇒N. [JUDGEMENT, CP18 text unseen] this is likely what CP18 hit.
- B2-strong [FAIL]: "no finite-window argument can ever exclude an infinite object" — refuted by induction, descent, bound+check, and the cycle equation.
- [JUDGEMENT] CP18 generalises ONLY to same-quantifier-shape arguments with no bridge (no height, bound, equation, or correct-space compactness) — not to all finite-window methods. It bites the current chain and would survive even a proof of the target (uniformity still missing), so it is the more durable barrier for divergence.

## Literature barriers

- Conway (1972) / Kurtz–Simon [PROOF, qualitative, HIGH confidence]: undecidability/hardness quantified OVER parametrised families, not over fixed 3n+1. Family-hardness ⇏ member-hardness (cf. MRDP vs. x²+y²=z²) [PROOF by logic]. Verdict [JUDGEMENT, MEDIUM-HIGH]: NOT a barrier to this programme; over-cited. Moral reverses: proof must use 3-specific facts — which are exactly assets A1/A3/A4. Exact complexity classes not vouched here.
- Tao ceiling [JUDGEMENT]: frontier, not impossibility proof.
- Fourier ≥1/2 obstruction [PROOF, as briefed]: genuine permanent shape constraint.

## Cycles — the loud finding

[JUDGEMENT, built on PROOFs] Cycle exclusion is genuinely more tractable and the programme undervalues its fit: a length-m cycle is fully captured by window m plus `(2ᵐ−3ᵏ)n = B_w` [PROOF from A1]; integrality `n = B_w/(2ᵐ−3ᵏ) ∈ N` IS the explicit transfer B2 demands elsewhere; the literature already runs mixing-plus-rigidity for cycles. A1–A4 are the rigid half of that pattern. Retargeting the mixing target as cycle-bound input replaces the missing bridge with one that exists. This is the headline pivot.

## What survives with barriers intact

Proved mixing inequality as its own theorem; cycle-restricted every-case results (highest value/effort); quantitative almost-all refinements; proved obstructions (Fourier/A7/A9 line); a conditional "mixing + hitting/descent ⇒ no divergence" specification; human + Lean re-verification of A1–A8 (with zero human review so far, undetected error is the largest near-term risk, not B1/B2).

On the lead's "NO measurable progress": [JUDGEMENT] about right for divergence, too harsh for cycles, lemma stock, and obstructions. "Cannot reach stated goal via mixing alone; should retarget" is available as a first-class result.

